1775367447
U: Investigate why two multi-color tennis courts behave differently in court detection pipeline. V1 (real_match_10min) fails on some frames detecting only green, while V2 (courtside_match_2) works despite also showing SINGLE color detection.
S: Performed visual analysis of 3 diagnostic images and ran quantitative color analysis script. Found the root cause: V1's blue surface has low saturation (S≈43, below SAT_COURT_THRESHOLD=50) so the saturation court mask covers only 15-24% of blue area. V2's blue has high saturation (S≈78) so the mask covers 93-95%. Lines on V1's blue surface fail the neighbor test because they lack court-mask support. The single differentiator is blue surface saturation relative to the S>50 threshold.
Read diagnostic images, ran color analysis Python script, grepped pipeline source for threshold constants
