1775374580
U: Rigorous comparison of two approaches for tennis court line detection: Approach A (color-based Agrawal + saturation-based + scoring with ~15 global thresholds) vs Approach B (proposed local-contrast via V top-hat + S black-hat with physics-grounded parameters).
S: Created comprehensive analysis at tennis-vision/analysis_line_detection_approaches.md. Explored codebase to understand actual implementation (thresholds, morphological operations, scoring logic). Analyzed both approaches across 12 court conditions + 4 cross-cutting concerns. Approach B wins or ties in 15/16 categories. Only Approach A edge: adjacent court filtering (low confidence, marginal). Key B advantages: no global color thresholds, no V>150 gate (works in shadows/low light), better scuff mark discrimination via dual criterion, ~3x faster (1 candidate vs 3), graceful degradation vs categorical failure. Recommended implementation path: B as primary with saturation fallback during validation.
Created: analysis_line_detection_approaches.md (analysis document, no code changes)
