1775379802
U: User asked for the best geometric constraints for service line detection, including pickleball court discrimination, and shared a reference image showing pickleball lines overlaid on a tennis court.
S: Proposed 6 geometric constraints for service line detection: (1) y-position band [0.20-0.60], (2) width ≤ baseline, (3) angle within 10° of baseline, (4) endpoint proximity to singles sidelines when detected, (5) width ratio check [0.55-0.85], (6) selection by closest to expected y instead of longest. Also proposed reordering identification to baseline→sidelines→service line. Analyzed pickleball discrimination showing Constraint 4 (endpoint proximity) is the key discriminator since pickleball lines at 6.1m are 1.065m inside the tennis singles sidelines at 8.23m.
