1775381024
U: User asked why the blue service line in panel 3 extends to the pillar when panel 4 shows no line pixels there.
S: Diagnosed why service line Hough segment extends to the pillar: merge_collinear_segments merges segments that are collinear (same angle, small perpendicular distance) but has no maximum gap constraint along the line direction. Two segments 500px apart get merged into one super-long segment. This is also the root cause of frame 900's extending service line.
Reviewed merge_collinear_segments lines 713-760
unknown

1775381407
U: User asked to investigate elegant solutions for the merge gap issue via subagent.
S: Subagent analysis complete. merge_collinear_segments called in 2 places with defaults (angle_tol=10, dist_tol=30). HoughLinesP uses maxLineGap=40 so separate segments already have >40px gaps. Recommended fix: add along-line gap check with max_gap=80px using interval merging within collinear groups. This rejects 400px+ false merges while preserving fragmented sideline merging.
Explored: merge_collinear_segments callers, detect_lines_near_half HoughLinesP params (maxLineGap=40)
